<p>Read <a href="/how-it-works/">our score inputs and limitations</a> and watch the <a href="/stress/apple-watch/#walkthrough">captioned development-build walkthrough with labeled sample data</a>. These explain our product; they do not prove accuracy against hormone tests.</p>
<h2 id="afib-history">Should I enable AFib History just to get more HRV readings?</h2>
<p><strong>No: do not enable it solely to improve a wellness app's data.</strong> <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-lamr/108375">Apple requires a physician diagnosis of atrial fibrillation for AFib History</a>. It is not a general-purpose stress-tracking setting. Use the features appropriate to your medical circumstances and record the data your Watch actually provides.</p>
<p>Our comparison checklist does not require changing this setting. More samples alone would not establish that an app measures cortisol or interprets your stress accurately.</p>
